{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.82,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": [
        "R78"
      ],
      "pins": [
        "R78.1",
        "R78.2"
      ],
      "nets": [
        "VOUTN",
        "VOUTP"
      ],
      "observed": "R78 is placed between VOUTN and VOUTP and is given the schematic value 24k, but its MPN and description identify a 24Ω resistor.",
      "expected": "For a two-terminal passive, the value, MPN, and description should agree. The circuit position is a high-value clamp/bleeder across the bridge-rectifier output, where 24k is consistent with the schematic value and SPICE deck; 24Ω would be orders of magnitude too low.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R78\") (value \"24k\") ... (field (name \"MPN\") \"FRC0805J240TSD\") ... (description \" 125mW Thick Film Resistors 150V ±100ppm/℃ ±5% 24Ω 0805 Chip Resistor - Surface Mount ROHS\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "R78 VOUTN VOUTP 24k"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the board is assembled from the MPN/description (24Ω) rather than the schematic value (24k), R78 would load VOUTP/VOUTN heavily, possibly overheating or failing and changing the intended clamp/bleeder behavior.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain a clear passive-component mismatch: R78 is specified as 24k in the schematic/SPICE but its MPN and description denote 24Ω, which would materially change the circuit if sourced from the BOM fields."
}

